NXR-160|Portable source handoff and dependency diagnosis|Tooling|The project shall preserve reachable Git history and current nonignored local source state in a verified portable archive and diagnose selected build dependencies through native C# tooling and CMake targets.|Development must continue on another computer without losing uncommitted DMA work or relying on old build caches.|A fixture restores staged unstaged untracked and deleted files and rejects tampering; actual handoff audit compares restored HEAD index and source hashes; dependency failures return nonzero.|Native handoff self-test, real archive restoration, dependency doctor and strict documentation build.|NXR-159|Native AOT default with managed fallback; host docs analysis ARM RISC-V RTL profiles are explicit.|Host tooling only; zero firmware RAM or flash cost.|tools/NexRT.Handoff/Program.cs,tools/NexRT.Handoff/Archive.cs,tools/NexRT.Handoff/Doctor.cs,cmake/dependencies.cmake,docs/handoff.rst|Sources and selected Linux runtime support are portable; compiler installations and machine credentials are excluded. Destination execution and hardware qualification remain machine-specific.|tools/NexRT.Handoff/Program.cs,tools/NexRT.Handoff/Archive.cs,tools/NexRT.Handoff/Doctor.cs,cmake/dependencies.cmake|tools/NexRT.Handoff/Archive.cs|PartialSourceUnverified
